## Summary

**Created**: `Game Design Document/Gameplay Rules/Entity System Rules.md` — a comprehensive 200-series rules document formalizing the Entity System.

### What was drafted (42 rules across 8 sections):

| Section | Rules | Covers |
|---|---|---|
| **200 Entities & Tags** | 200.1–200.3 | Entity definition, Tag categories, Object References (Own/Other/Any, Faction Relationships) |
| **210 Characteristics** | 210.1–210.7c | Statline (Endurance, Durability, Morale, Speed, Reflex), Morale state machine, derived Characteristics (Baseline Competence, Evasion Rating, Armour Value) |
| **220 Items** | 220.1–220.10 | Items, Item Types, Weapons, Attack Profiles, Range Brackets, Armour, Armour Resistances, Damage Types, Modifiers, Consumables |
| **230 Models** | 230.1–230.2 | Model definition, Bearer relationship |
| **240 Units** | 240.1–240.6 | Unit definition, Composition, Tag/State Inheritance, Datasheets, Unit Value |
| **250 Abilities** | 250.1–250.4 | Ability definition, Passive/Active/Surge types with rule statement templates |
| **260 Commanders** | 260.1–260.2 | Commander definition, Commander–Army relationship |
| **270 Armies & Battleforces** | 270.1–270.3 | Army, Battleforce, Rosters |

### Validation

Ran self-validation against the Rules Validator criteria. Fixed 2 errors (vague Damage Type descriptions, capitalization inconsistency) and addressed 5 warnings (removed "typically"/"some"/"most", clarified Surge triggers). Remaining warnings are intentional forward references to the not-yet-drafted Combat Resolution rules (400-series).

### Key learning

The `weapon_skill` field in `Units.json` has no counterpart in the terminology — it needs reconciliation when Combat Resolution rules are drafted.
